    "North is assumed up for the NASA/LROC overview; scale is read from its 2 km bar. Re-register against the controlled ortho before placing exact camera stations.",
    "Station 3 was a brief belt-sample stop, not completion of all its planned tasks. Planned unvisited stations must not become historical visits.",
    "ALSEP and final LRV markers are approximate bearing/range anchors from mission narrative; local driving, Grand Prix and individual sampling walks are not recoverable from this overview. Their operating areas fit the boundary.",
    "The narrow 2 m product misses part of the eastern margin and two mountain-front route vertices. The verified broader 5 m APOLLO15_2 footprint covers the proposed area; blend/resample after a confidence-mask audit, rather than inventing measured detail.",
    "Routes depict driven corridors; add bootprints only at documented walking work areas. No individual footprint placement is claimed.",
    "Per-pixel DTM confidence, shadow/interpolation artifacts, real surface grades, and precise image-station registration remain construction prerequisites.",
    "The source overview covers the mission region but cannot reconstruct every short movement within sampling sites. Operating disks reserve space without presenting invented paths."
